      answer: 'Choreography lets each service react to events independently with no central coordinator, avoiding a single point of coordination, but it distributes failure-handling logic across every consumer and makes the overall flow harder to trace when something goes wrong. Orchestration centralizes that logic in a saga coordinator that explicitly tracks each step and issues compensating actions, making failure handling traceable at the cost of the coordinator itself becoming a dependency that must be highly available.',
